   "id": "sotah.15a.6",
   "daf": "15a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וְאֵין אֲסוּרִין אֶלָּא מִלְּחַמֵּץ, דִּכְתִיב: ״לֹא תֵאָפֶה חָמֵץ חֶלְקָם״, אָמַר רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן לָקִישׁ: אֲפִילּוּ חֶלְקָם לֹא תֵאָפֶה חָמֵץ.",
   "en": "The baraita concludes: «And they are prohibited only from allowing» the meal-offering «to become leavened.» The Gemara cites the source: «As it is written» with regard to meal-offerings: «“It shall not be baked with leaven. Their portion» I have given it of My offerings made by fire” (Leviticus 6:10). «Rabbi Shimon ben Lakish says:» One should read the verse as if the phrase “their portion” is part of the same phrase as the prohibition of baking with leaven. This teaches that «even their portion,» i.e., the portion given to the priests, «shall not be baked with leaven.»"
  }
 ],
